{"id": "unknown-2026-10-09-009", "date": "2026-10-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Vietnam’s R&I credit rating rises to BBB- with stable outlook", "content": "Vietnam has entered investment grade for the first time after R&I raised its foreign-currency issuer rating to BBB- from BB+.\nThe outlook moved to stable from positive, with R&I citing growth fundamentals, reforms, fiscal space and shock resilience.\nThe finance ministry said the upgrade should support investor confidence and long-term capital mobilisation.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-s-r-i-credit-rating-rises-to-bbb-with-stable-outlook-314145-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-09-010", "date": "2026-10-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["expand", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh’s PMI falls to 48.6 in September as manufacturing contracts", "content": "Bangladesh’s PMI fell to 48.6 in September from 49.9 in August, as manufacturing and construction contracted and services remained weak. \nAgriculture continued to expand for the 13th consecutive month. \nBusinesses cited rising costs, fuel price hikes, energy shortages, weak consumer demand and limited credit access as major challenges.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-s-pmi-falls-to-48-6-in-september-as-manufacturing-contracts-314142-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-09-011", "date": "2026-10-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.75, "keywords": ["record", "growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "India targets $1 trn exports in current year: Goyal", "content": "India has set a $1 trillion export target for the current year after recording $863 billion in exports last year, Commerce and Industry Minister Piyush Goyal said in a summit.\nHe said the goal implies nearly 16 per cent growth, against expected global trade growth of about 2.5-3 per cent. \nGoyal urged CII to create FTA utilisation desks in every state council for MSMEs.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-targets-1-trn-exports-in-current-year-goyal-314134-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-09-012", "date": "2026-10-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.67, "keywords": ["decline", "slow", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "South Indian cotton yarn sees mixed trend as raw cotton costs rise", "content": "India’s cotton yarn markets were mixed, with Mumbai seeing ₹3–6 (~$0.03–0.06) per kg gains in several counts but ₹2–5 declines in selected varieties as weak fabric demand and payment constraints weighed on sentiment.\nTiruppur yarn rose ₹2–3 per kg as costlier cotton prompted stock replenishment.\nGujarat cotton jumped ₹1,500–2,000 per candy on firmer ICE futures and slower arrivals.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/south-indian-cotton-yarn-sees-mixed-trend-as-raw-cotton-costs-rise-314128-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-09-013", "date": "2026-10-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam & US close to finalising reciprocal trade agreement", "content": "Vietnam and the US have settled most of a reciprocal, fair and balanced trade agreement, with only technical issues left, the industry ministry said.\nSeven official rounds have been held since April 2025, alongside ministerial and technical-level talks.\nThe US was Vietnam's top export market at $140 billion in the first nine months; the surplus rose 23.8 per cent to $122.62 billion.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-us-close-to-finalising-reciprocal-trade-agreement-314125-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-09-014", "date": "2026-10-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "US Upland cotton export sales fall 19%; shipments rise 8%: USDA", "content": "US cotton export sales fell in the week ended October 1, 2026, with 2026–27 Upland net sales down 19 per cent week on week to 165,100 RB, though 14 per cent above the four-week average.\nVietnam led Upland buying at 61,800 RB, followed by Pakistan and India; Upland shipments rose 8 per cent to 161,600 RB.\nPima sales recovered to 3,300 RB, but shipments dropped 69 per cent to 2,900 RB.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/us-upland-cotton-export-sales-fall-19-shipments-rise-8-usda-314124-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-09-015", "date": "2026-10-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["record"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "ICE cotton futures edge lower ahead of USDA WASDE report", "content": "US ICE cotton futures settled marginally lower on Thursday as traders awaited the USDA WASDE report, with the December 2026 contract down 9 points at 79.94 cents per pound.\nThe contract stayed 106 points higher for the week, while volume eased to 40,731 lots and open interest remained near a record high.\nUS export sales totalled 224,404 bales, led by Vietnam, Pakistan, China and India.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-futures-edge-lower-ahead-of-usda-wasde-report-314116-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-09-016", "date": "2026-10-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.75, "keywords": ["decline", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Cambodia, Indonesia ship $5.6 bn in US apparel: China losing ground?", "content": "Cambodia and Indonesia supplied $5.60 billion of US apparel imports in January-July 2026, overtaking China’s $5.28 billion as the US market contracted.\nTexPro data shows imports fell 8.30 per cent to $44.06 billion, with China and India driving most of the net decline.\nGains came mainly from stronger category positions, but value pressure and textile dependencies remain risks.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/cambodia-indonesia-ship-5-6-bn-in-us-apparel-china-losing-ground--314126-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
